            <td height="336"> 
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">It 
                has now been more than one year since PMWatch (along with many 
                other groups) started communicating on a regular basis with all 
                the major media outlets -- CNN, NPR, The New York Times, The Washington 
                Post, The Philadelphia Inquirer, The Boston Globe, etc. -- providing 
                them with compelling evidence showing how their media coverage 
                on the Palestinian-Israeli conflict is deeply rooted in the Israeli 
                narrative and grossly neglectful of the Palestinian narrative. 
                (See our <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/reports/index.html">reports</a> for details)</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">The 
                media has responded here and there with some minor adjustments, 
                offering a little more access to their op-ed pages, showing a 
                bit more care in not adopting wholesale the language of the Israeli 
                Prime Minister's Office, but by and large, if one reads the editorials 
                emanating from all the major outlets, or examines the news stories 
                coming out on the conflict, it is quite clear that the standard 
                narrative is basically intact: the Palestinians started it all, 
                the are responsible for the lion's share of the violence, and 
                they are the ones who should be pressured to calm things down.</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Below 
                is a list of the major grievances against the US media's coverage 
                of the conflict. Please add your comments if you wish and just 
                click on the 'Send' button, and the message below will be sent 
                to all the major media outlets, print as well as electronic. If 
                the media won't listen to our patient reasoning, maybe they will 
                listen when hundreds of people raise their voice in protest over 
                their shameless irresponsibility.</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Please 
                make sure that your email address and name are correct. </font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Palestine 
                Media Watch - <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/index.html" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">http://www.pmwatch.org</a></font></p>
            </td>
